{
  "_comment": [
    "Template for an agent's tool-server configuration (MCP or equivalent). Copy to the path your",
    "runtime expects, git-ignore the live copy, and commit ONLY this template.",
    "",
    "THE RULE THAT CATCHES EVERYONE: values written as ${VAR} are expanded from the PROCESS",
    "ENVIRONMENT, not from a .env file. Nothing loads .env for you. Populating that file alone leaves",
    "servers reporting missing credentials while the values sit right there — export them first:",
    "",
    "    set -a; . ./.env; set +a      # then start your editor or agent FROM THAT SHELL",
    "",
    "Choose servers by what they let an agent DO that it otherwise cannot. Each one is attack surface",
    "and context budget, so a server nobody uses is a cost with no benefit."
  ],

  "servers": {
    "_repository_host": {
      "_why": "Read and write pull requests, issues and reviews. The single highest-value server: it is what lets an agent finish a task rather than hand you a diff.",
      "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "<github-or-gitlab-mcp-server>"],
      "env": { "TOKEN": "${REPO_TOKEN}" }
    },
    "_code_intelligence": {
      "_why": "A queryable graph of the codebase — call chains, blast radius before a change. Use it to SCOPE work: what calls this, what breaks if it changes. Prefer one that runs locally with no code egress.",
      "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "<code-graph-server>"]
    },
    "_browser": {
      "_why": "Drive a real browser for UI verification and accessibility checks. Only useful once you have a user-facing surface — before that it is unused context.",
      "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "<browser-automation-server>"]
    },
    "_issue_tracker": {
      "_why": "Read the ticket an agent is implementing, and file the issue a blocked decision needs.",
      "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "<tracker-server>"],
      "env": { "TOKEN": "${TRACKER_TOKEN}" }
    },
    "_docs_or_notes": {
      "_why": "Read the design source of record, so grounding is a tool call rather than a paste.",
      "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "<notes-server>"]
    }
  },

  "_operational_notes": [
    "VERIFY, DO NOT ASSUME. Whatever your runtime's 'list servers' command is, run it and read the",
    "status. A server can be configured, connected, AND unauthenticated all at once — which looks",
    "healthy and fails on first real use.",
    "",
    "WATCH FOR DUPLICATE SCOPES. The same server defined at both user and project scope with different",
    "endpoints will split authentication state, and you will authenticate one and use the other.",
    "",
    "REMOVE WHAT YOU DO NOT USE. Every server costs context and adds a failure mode."
  ]
}
